<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds closed well-supported, with the market shrugging off the absence of a widely-predicted cut in the Bank of Portugal's drain rate.</p>
<p>The spread with the German Bunds in the 10-year cash sector was seen remaining around 90 basis points.</p>
<p>&quot;Futures closed firmer and cash were at record highs, completely indifferent to the fact that the Bank of Portugal did not cut.</p>
<p>&quot;The positive sentiment is going to continue strong,&quot; said one trader.</p>
</text>
